{"chunk_id": "cfc047b6498c", "text": "This section recounts the divine births of the first two Pandavas and the events leading toward the birth of a third. At Pandu\u2019s request, Kunti uses the sacred incantation given by the sage Durvasa to summon the god of justice, Dharma. From their union is born Yudhishthira, foretold by a heavenly voice to be the most virtuous of men and a future ruler. Pandu then asks for a son of immense physical power, leading Kunti to invoke Vayu, the wind-god, who fathers Bhima. Bhima\u2019s extraordinary strength is revealed immediately when he falls from Kunti\u2019s lap and shatters a rock without harm. Significantly, Bhima is born on the same day as Duryodhana. Pandu then resolves to obtain an even greater son through austerities to please Indra, foreshadowing the birth of Arjuna.\nKunti invokes gods to bear sons for Pandu, giving birth to Yudhishthira and Bhima, while Pandu begins austerities seeking a third heroic son from Indra.\nThemes: divine conception, birth of heroes, destiny and prophecy, ascetic devotion, Kuru lineage", "vector": [0.0015281757805496454, -0.028369802981615067, -0.025321699678897858, 0.005763028748333454, -0.0159530658274889, 0.024318858981132507, -0.012660849839448929, -0.0015224028611555696, -0.015557208098471165, -0.03293536230921745, 0.0032955154310911894, 0.011361116543412209, 0.008207449689507484, 0.015174546279013157, -0.007903959602117538, 0.010820111259818077, 0.033806249499320984, -0.004288458731025457, 0.026905130594968796, -0.014145315624773502, -0.012324370443820953, -0.025189746171236038, 0.012852180749177933, 0.017800401896238327, -0.02813228778541088, 0.030481044203042984, 0.022959748283028603, -0.016058627516031265, 0.008233840577304363, -0.009619342163205147, -0.020782530307769775, 0.008675881661474705, 0.00904534850269556, 0.0003397778782527894, -0.023513948544859886, 0.002582971705123782, 0.007336562965065241, -0.023355605080723763, 0.014871055260300636, -0.007778604049235582, 0.014422416